    "result_text": "I've verified the full picture. Every rejection path in the application flows through a checked exception to an escalation handler \u2014 there are **no** 400/409/429 responses produced outside those handlers (the only `ResponseEntity.status(...)` calls in function classes are success responses: 201/204/302).\n\nReviewing each rejection handler confirms they already emit RFC7807 `application/problem+json` via the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper:\n\n| Handler | Status | Body |\n|---|---|---|\n| `OwnerFieldsInvalidExceptionHandler` | 400 | `ProblemDetail` |\n| `ValidationExceptionHandler` (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`) | 400 | `ProblemDetail` |\n| `OwnerIdentityConflictExceptionHandler` | 409 | `ProblemDetail` |\n| `OwnerHouseholdConflictExceptionHandler` | 409 | `ProblemDetail` |\n| `OwnerCityCapacityConflictExceptionHandler` | 409 | `ProblemDetail` |\n| `OwnerDailyCreateLimitExceptionHandler` | 429 | `ProblemDetail` |\n\n`ProblemDetails.build` sets `type` (`about:blank`), `title` (exception simple name), the `status`, and `detail` \u2014 all four required RFC7807 members \u2014 and the handlers return `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>`, which OfficeFloor serializes with the `application/problem+json` content type (confirmed green by the new `Cp59Tests`).\n\nI ran the suites:\n\n- **`Cp59Tests`** (the new problem-json checkpoint) \u2192 passes: asserts `400`, `application/problem+json`, and `$.status == 400`.\n- **Full `./mvnw -o test`** \u2192 `Tests run: 71, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nThe specification is already fully satisfied by the working tree: all 400/409/429 rejections return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`, with HTTP status codes unchanged. The entire test suite (existing + new) is green, so no code changes were required. I did not fabricate edits given the implementation was already complete and verified.",
